# Architecture

Reuse existing contracts. Do not invent competing models, services, or
abstractions. Inspect `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/decisions/`, and the
matching domain/application modules before changing behavior.

Layer responsibilities:

- `src/agentic_portfolio_lab/domain` — deterministic models, invariants, math
- `src/agentic_portfolio_lab/application` — workflows, services, orchestration
- `src/agentic_portfolio_lab/infrastructure` — providers, SQLite, external adapters
- `src/agentic_portfolio_lab/api` — transport and serialization only
- `frontend/` — presentation and operator commands only

FastAPI must not own portfolio, recommendation, validation, benchmark,
execution, or financial-calculation policy. Streamlit is a diagnostic demo UI,
not the v0.1 operator loop.

## Managed decision lineage

Keep this chain intact and auditable:

`ResearchBatch` → `decision_cycle_id` → recommendation → deterministic
validation → journal → approval → execution/history

Managers produce intent only (ADR-003). They never execute or mutate
portfolios.

## Benchmark lineage (separate)

Keep funding and benchmark fulfillment off the managed execution path:

paired Cash Event funding → benchmark fulfillment → benchmark history

Canonical SPY identity is `SPY` / `NYSE ARCA` / `ETF` / `USD`. Provider
identity translation stays at adapter boundaries. See ADR-001, ADR-002, and
ADR-006.
